---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy notice · Handsdown"
  description="What Blureffect stores when you share your details, why, who else sees it, and how to have it deleted."
  ogTitle="Privacy notice"
>
  <main class="mx-auto w-full max-w-[68ch] px-6 py-20 sm:py-28">
    <p class="eyebrow text-text-tertiary">Privacy notice</p>
    <h1 class="mt-4 text-[clamp(30px,4vw,44px)] font-bold leading-tight tracking-[-0.02em] text-text-primary">
      What we store, and how to have it deleted
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-text-tertiary">
      Version 2026-10-d · in effect since 2026-10-30
    </p>
    <div class="mt-10 space-y-5">
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        Who we are. This website and its chat are run by Blur Effect LLC, 103
        Capitol Ave, Suite 420A, Cheyenne, WY 82001, United States
        ("Blureffect", "we"), which offers the Handsdown service. We decide how
        your data is used. You can reach us at info@blureffect.co.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        This notice covers what you share with Blureffect on this website, in
        its forms and in the chat with our AI agent. We store and process it in
        the United States, on Amazon Web Services (AWS) in its us-east-1 region.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        We store the name, work email, company and role description you share
        with us so that our sales team can contact you about hiring engineers
        through Blureffect, and so we can prepare that conversation.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        The chat on this website is an AI agent, not a person, and any face or
        voice it uses is computer-generated. It stores what you type with the
        conversation, so it can answer you and so our team can follow up.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        The microphone stays off until you allow it. When you use it, your
        browser turns your speech into text and the agent receives only that
        text, never audio. To do that, your browser may send your voice to a
        speech service run by the company that makes it (for example Google in
        Chrome, or Apple in Safari), under the terms of that company. Once we
        switch on Deepgram (described below), your browser will send your voice
        to Deepgram instead, and the agent will still receive only text.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        Why we use your data, and our legal basis for each use:
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        To answer you in the chat and on this site, and to keep the conversation
        for 24 hours: our legitimate interest in answering people who contact
        us.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        To contact you about hiring engineers once you give us your details and
        agree: your consent, which you can withdraw at any time.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        Once we switch on TypeSafe AI (described below), to test whether
        prepared answers could answer common first questions: our legitimate
        interest in measuring and improving the chat.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        To keep proof of the choices you make about the microphone and about
        being contacted: our legitimate interest in being able to show that we
        respected them.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        To keep the site secure and stop abuse: our legitimate interest in
        security.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        If you apply to join our network of specialists, to evaluate your
        application and to contact you about roles that fit it: the steps you
        ask us to take before we work together.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        A chat conversation is deleted automatically 24 hours after it starts.
        Contact details the chat agent records for us are deleted after 30 days
        unless you agree to be contacted. Details you give us in a form, or
        agree to us keeping, are kept as a lead for 24 months after you last
        contacted us, unless you ask us to delete them sooner. The brief you
        type into Smart Match, and a position you send us for review, are kept
        until you ask us to delete them. Once we switch it on, TypeSafe AI may
        keep the text of your first chat message, as described below, for as
        long as its terms allow.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        An application to join our network, and the CV you send with it, are
        kept for 24 months after you send it, unless you ask us to delete them
        sooner. A CV you upload but never send with an application is deleted
        after one day.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        A record of each choice you make about the microphone is kept for 3
        years as proof, even after the conversation is deleted. It holds the
        conversation's reference, the choice, the version of the text you saw
        and the time, and no name, email address or message.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        If your details had already reached another company when we delete them,
        we keep a record of the deletion so that copy can still be found and
        erased. It holds a one-way code made from your email address, the
        version of the notice you accepted and the dates, and no name or
        message.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        These companies receive your data to do their part of that work. Each is
        named below with what it receives, and with what deleting a chat
        conversation does not reach there. A company that starts with "When we
        switch it on" receives nothing today.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        AWS runs our servers and databases and stores everything this notice
        describes. Deleting the conversation removes it from our database at
        AWS, but not from backups and operational logs that may hold parts of it
        until they expire (our operational logs at AWS expire after 14 days),
        and it does not erase the contact details it saved as a lead or the
        record of your microphone choices described above.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        Anthropic provides the language model behind the chat agent and the
        Smart Match search. It receives what you write to either of them so the
        model can respond, and in the chat also the conversation so far.
        Deleting the conversation does not reach any copy Anthropic keeps under
        its own terms. If you apply to join our network and upload a CV,
        Anthropic also receives the CV's text, so the model can fill in your
        application. Deleting your application does not reach any copy of that
        text Anthropic keeps under its own terms either.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        When we switch it on, Deepgram will turn the chat agent's written
        answers into its spoken voice, and will receive the text of those
        answers, which can repeat things you wrote, such as a name or a company.
        If you use the microphone, your browser will send your voice directly to
        Deepgram, which turns it into text, and we will receive only that text,
        never audio. Every one of these requests opts out of Deepgram's Model
        Improvement Program. Deleting the conversation does not reach Deepgram,
        which says it keeps a request that opts out of that program only as long
        as it needs to process it.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        When we switch it on, TypeSafe AI may receive the text of your first
        message to the chat agent, with email addresses, phone numbers and web
        addresses removed and no account, session or device identifier attached,
        so that its model can pick a prepared answer. Anything else in that
        message, such as a name or a company, is not removed. Under its terms
        TypeSafe AI may keep that text and use it to run and improve its own
        services. Deleting the conversation does not reach the copy of that
        first message TypeSafe AI may keep for as long as its terms allow.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        HubSpot, our sales CRM, receives your name, work email, phone number and
        company, and a deal record with our estimate of how well the role fits
        our service, so our sales team can follow up. Deleting the conversation
        does not erase what HubSpot already holds; write to info@blureffect.co
        and we will erase it there.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        When we switch it on, Chatwoot Inc. will run the inbox our team uses
        when a conversation is handed to a person, and will receive the messages
        of that conversation when that happens. Deleting the conversation will
        also remove its copy from our Chatwoot inbox.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        When we switch it on, Voyage AI will receive search text based on what
        you write to the chat agent, to find passages in our own documents that
        can answer you. Deleting the conversation does not reach any copy of
        that search text Voyage AI keeps under its own terms.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        When we switch it on, Cohere will receive the same search text when the
        agent ranks those passages by how well they answer you. Deleting the
        conversation does not reach any copy of that search text Cohere keeps
        under its own terms.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        When we switch it on, Google will receive your name and email address in
        the invitation when you book a meeting with us through Google Workspace
        Calendar. Deleting the conversation does not cancel a meeting already
        booked in Google Workspace Calendar.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        SendGrid delivers the emails we send you, such as confirmations and
        match reports, and receives your email address and the content of each
        email. Deleting the conversation does not reach an email already sent
        through SendGrid, or the record SendGrid keeps of it.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        When we switch it on, Slack will carry the alert that tells our sales
        team about a new lead, with your name, email address, company and what
        you told us about the role. Deleting the conversation does not remove an
        alert already posted to our team channel in Slack.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        When we switch it on, Cloudflare will check that you are not a bot
        before a chat starts or a position search is activated, and will receive
        your IP address and technical details about your browser for that check.
        Deleting the conversation does not reach anything Cloudflare keeps from
        these checks under its own terms.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        Vercel is a hosting service that delivers this website at some of its
        addresses, and receives every request your browser sends through them,
        including what you type into forms and the chat. Deleting the
        conversation does not reach anything Vercel keeps from those requests
        under its own terms.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        When we switch it on, Cal.com will receive the name, email address and
        answers you enter when you book a call through the calendar on our
        booking page, with identifiers that link the booking to your visit.
        Deleting the conversation does not cancel a call booked through Cal.com
        or erase what you entered there.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        Two public DNS services also see the domain of your work email when we
        check that the address can receive mail: Cloudflare's (1.1.1.1) and
        Google's (8.8.8.8). They receive only the domain, not the address, and
        handle it as independent companies under their own privacy policies, not
        on our behalf.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        When your data leaves the European Union or the United Kingdom, the law
        requires a safeguard: the Standard Contractual Clauses approved by the
        European Commission (with the UK Addendum for data from the United
        Kingdom), written into our data processing agreement with the company,
        or the company's certification under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework
        and its UK Extension. When we switch on TypeSafe AI, it will rely on the
        Standard Contractual Clauses in its data processing addendum. Write to
        info@blureffect.co to ask which safeguard applies to a company, or for a
        copy.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        What we store in your browser. The chat keeps a session key in your
        browser so that moving between pages does not lose the conversation; it
        expires after 24 hours. It also keeps a visit identifier for as long as
        the tab is open. Our website stores a random identifier to count visits
        and see which pages lead to a booked call, and links it to your details
        if you later give them to us. It also keeps the Smart Match brief you
        type for 48 hours so a reload does not lose it, the answers of a brief
        in progress until you close the tab, and a random key that lets this
        browser answer our consent request for the details it sent. If you apply
        to join our network of specialists, the application keeps your answers
        in this browser as you go, so you can finish later, until you send it or
        press Erase my answers.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        Please do not share sensitive information, such as health details, in
        the chat. We use what you tell us about the role to estimate how well it
        fits our service so our sales team can prioritise; no decision with
        legal or similarly significant effects is made about you automatically.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        Your rights. You can ask us for a copy of your data, to correct it, to
        delete it, to limit how we use it, or to receive it in a portable
        format, by writing to info@blureffect.co. We answer within one month.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        Your right to object. Where we rely on our legitimate interest, you can
        object at any time by writing to info@blureffect.co, and we will stop
        unless we have compelling reasons that override yours.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        You can also complain to a data protection authority, in particular in
        the European Union country where you live or work, or in the United
        Kingdom to the Information Commissioner's Office (ico.org.uk).
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        You can delete a chat conversation at any time from the menu in the chat
        header. For everything else, write to info@blureffect.co. You can
        withdraw your consent and ask us to delete your data at any time.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        If you decline when we ask for your consent, we delete the details this
        browser submitted, and none of them are copied to HubSpot. Declining
        does not delete a chat conversation, which you can delete from the chat
        itself, or anything already sent to the companies named above.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-12 border-t border-border-default pt-8 text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
      To ask what we hold about you, or to have it deleted, write to{" "}
      <a
        href="mailto:info@blureffect.co"
        class="font-medium text-text-accent underline underline-offset-4 focus-visible:shadow-ring focus-visible:outline-none"
      >
        info@blureffect.co
      </a>
      .
    </p>
  </main>
</Base>
